        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A TRUE treadmill is a heavy, dealer-installed machine from a
          commercial maker, and the Performance 1000 is the one most home runners should start
          with.</strong> The Z500 suits walkers short of space, the 3000 adds a softer belt, and the
          8000 adds an adjustable deck and the longest parts cover, but none is faster or stronger than
          the 1000.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy from an authorised dealer or TRUE's store, pay for installation so the warranty stands,
          and compare quotes on the same console, because the same model varied by $1,000 between
          sellers on the day we checked. If you are cross-shopping, our
          <a href="/spirit-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Spirit guide</a>
